-- ── Hypotheses ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- H1: PLAN EQUALITY on the base five. The catalog-driven base_estimate
-- ((PredicateDecl, pattern) with PredicateStats.live_facts populated at plan
-- time from the derive Stats oracle) and the plan-time (PredicateId, SortOrder)
-- base-leg resolution produce RulePlans IDENTICAL to HEAD's on (i) the plan.rs
-- fixture programs and (ii) every bundled stdlib pack (evaluated composition),
-- under both stats profiles — pinned by the committed golden fingerprints
-- (struct-level render: literal, pattern, source kind+surface name, join,
-- estimate, head_domains; not mere acceptance). Ground: with distinct[i] = 0
-- and max_fanout = 0 (the pre-compaction state) the generalized formulas are
-- DEFINED to emit exactly today's narrowed_fanout / avg_degree / per-type
-- oracle values, and live_facts is populated with exactly the magnitudes the
-- old formulas read (node/type/attr -> total_nodes, edge/incoming ->
-- total_edges).
claim_of[a](exp_p3_plan_equality_golden).
ground[a](exp_p3_plan_equality_golden, unknown_stats_fallbacks_defined_equal_to_head_formulas).
expected[m](exp_p3_plan_equality_golden, golden_fingerprints_bit_identical_pre_and_post).

-- H2: the two HISTORICAL estimator regression classes stay mechanically dead,
-- pinned by formula-verbatim unit tests over every (base-five relation x bind
-- pattern) on a populated Stats:
--   * bound-endpoint adjacency = avg-degree ceil(E/N), NOT sqrt(E) — the ~300x
--     hop inflation (920 vs ~3; 3-hop chain 779M = spurious E-PLAN-003);
--   * const-edge-type narrowing = narrowed_fanout(total_edges) — the depends
--     54M-vs-1.6k IMPORTS_FROM class;
--   * attr bound-id = 1; attr key+value = doubly-narrowed; node const-type =
--     per-type oracle including absent-type ~0.
-- E-PLAN-003 remains an availability HARD REJECT: zero E-PLAN-003 on the three
-- real packs (H6) regardless of timing.
claim_of[a](exp_p3_estimator_regressions_pinned).
ground[a](exp_p3_estimator_regressions_pinned, formula_verbatim_unit_battery_per_relation_per_pattern).
expected[m](exp_p3_estimator_regressions_pinned, new_base_estimate_equals_old_formula_output_verbatim).

-- H3: E-CAT-002 lands, with ONE evidence-forced scoping DEVIATION from the
-- spec's case (a), registered here BEFORE implementation:
--   SPEC case (a) as written ("positive body atom naming an unregistered
--   non-builtin predicate -> plan-time E-CAT-002") is UNIMPLEMENTABLE without
--   breaking two hard gates of the same spec:
--     * the ROFL F2 fix is regression-pinned: a body literal over a predicate
--       with no facts and no rules is a LEGAL EMPTY relation
--       (exec.rs::unknown_predicate_leg_terminates_with_empty_result and
--       ..._expired_deadline_aborts_with_e_exec_001; harness
--       translate.ts:329-331 states it verbatim and renderDumpSource depends
--       on it for factless rels);
--     * 12 of the 120 tier-0 seeds contain a body literal on a relation with
--       ZERO defining lines (measured on the committed generator: seeds 22,
--       31, 42, 43, 55, 76, 81, 82, 85, 88, 97, 117 — seed 97/117 in a
--       NEGATED position), and the tier-0 baseline 120/0 is a hard gate (5);
--     * the doc itself (§3.1) normatively grants undeclared predicates the
--       DEFAULT declaration ("новый предикат не требует ничьего разрешения").
--   RESOLUTION (recorded, not silent): a body-only predicate at a CONSISTENT
--   arity is REGISTERED at plan time via the §3.1 default rule and classified
--   as a legal, catalog-registered EMPTY relation served by the derived-
--   relation path's missing-relation arm — NEVER by exec.rs:1960-1967's
--   unknown-name fallback. E-CAT-002 fires at plan time for:
--     (a-scoped) a program predicate used at an arity CONFLICTING with its
--       catalog declaration — body-only names used at two arities in one
--       program (today: silently empty), and rule HEADS conflicting with an
--       existing decl;
--     (b) strict head validation per ledger round-005 C3 — INCLUDING a head
--       shadowing a base-relation name at a different arity (edge/1 over base
--       edge/3): the base_shadowing_head_still_plans_and_registers_nothing_new
--       pin is CONSCIOUSLY FLIPPED to expect E-CAT-002. Verified pre-flip: no
--       bundled stdlib pack and no tier-0 seed heads a base-relation name
--       (grep of all 43 .dl heads; tier-0 heads are p0-p3/q0-q2);
--     (d) the FactStore read path: unknown CatalogPredicateId in
--       sorted_run/prefix_scan migrates E-CAT-001 -> E-CAT-002 (round-007-pre
--       C10), facts:: tests updated.
--   CONSEQUENCE for the silent-wrong class: after P3 every predicate name
--   reaching the executor is either storage-served (Base), registered-derived
--   (rules or the §3.1 default = explicit empty), or a registry builtin; the
--   exec.rs:1960-1967 lookup-miss branch is reachable ONLY for the closed
--   query-engine-shared function set {path, parent_function, resolved_import}
--   (debug-asserted and documented) — the UNREGISTERED-predicate silently-
--   empty/vacuous-negation class is dead by construction.
claim_of[a](exp_p3_ecat002_scoped_and_landed).
ground[a](exp_p3_ecat002_scoped_and_landed, f2_pin_plus_12_tier0_seeds_plus_doc_3_1_default_rule).
expected[m](exp_p3_ecat002_scoped_and_landed, ecat002_fires_on_arity_conflict_head_strict_and_read_path_yet_tier0_stays_120_0).

-- H4: build-once dispatch generalizes to ONE form keyed
-- (PredicateId, SortOrder, bound_column_mask); the four existing
-- implementations (edge/incoming bound-probe, node membership, attr bound-id,
-- edge_attr) plus the cached free generators and the anti-join set builder
-- become instances selected from the plan-resolved key, NOT from string names:
--   * the type->node alias (exec.rs:1958, :1710) dissolves — a `type` leg is
--     plan-resolved to node's PredicateId;
--   * `incoming` is plan-resolved to edge's PredicateId + SortOrder::Reverse
--     (§6.3: incoming IS edge's reverse run); the catalog KEEPS the P2 alias
--     decls for the facts layer (Q4 explicitly allows either; the physical
--     de-aliasing is P6), and additionally maps name -> (id, order) for
--     dispatch;
--   * edge_attr (a builtin Function with a build-once arm) keeps an EXPLICITLY
--     DOCUMENTED builtin-side dispatch per Q2's allowance;
--   * emission byte-identical: the A/B battery (with_build_once_min_rows 0 vs
--     usize::MAX) extended over the migrated dispatch; an `incoming` leg and
--     the equivalent edge-Reverse resolution produce identical tuples;
--   * the ~240us/probe per-row fallback stays the correctness floor.
claim_of[a](exp_p3_dispatch_generalized).
ground[a](exp_p3_dispatch_generalized, four_instances_one_key_ab_multiset_equality).
expected[m](exp_p3_dispatch_generalized, fast_vs_per_row_byte_identical_and_incoming_equals_edge_reverse).

-- H5: PredicateStats populated at PLAN time from the existing cached oracles
-- (Q1 resolution): live_facts/live_asserts <- {node,type,attr: total_nodes;
-- edge,incoming: total_edges} from the engine's version+tombstone-keyed
-- derive_stats cache — ZERO added per-plan storage cost (engine_v2.rs is NOT
-- touched); distinct/max_fanout stay 0 and updated_at_tx stays 0 = "compaction
-- stats never computed" (P6 owns them, with manifest persistence). The
-- estimator gates its distinct-branch on distinct[i] > 0, so the P3 state
-- provably reproduces the fallbacks (H1).
claim_of[a](exp_p3_stats_from_plan_time_oracles).
ground[a](exp_p3_stats_from_plan_time_oracles, derive_stats_cache_is_the_feed_no_engine_change).
expected[m](exp_p3_stats_from_plan_time_oracles, live_facts_populated_distinct_zero_updated_at_tx_zero).

-- H6: perf proxy (the bounded stand-in for doc C6's 56.2s-warm pack fence).
-- Post-P3, 3 runs of p3_pack_baseline_on_real_corpus: per-pack MEDIAN <=
-- 1.10x the pre-P3 medians (<= 5.46 / 9.44 / 6.07 s); ANY E-PLAN-003 on these
-- packs is a HARD FAIL regardless of timing (availability — the doc's
-- regression class). depends_dl_maintain_vs_full_on_real_corpus run once:
-- maintain stays < full. Caveat carried from the baseline: write-back is
-- (+0,-0) on the pre-materialized copy — the timed work is parse+plan+join+
-- diff, which is exactly the derive-path cost C6 polices.
claim_of[a](exp_p3_perf_proxy_within_fence).
ground[a](exp_p3_perf_proxy_within_fence, same_command_same_base_median_of_three).
expected[m](exp_p3_perf_proxy_within_fence, medians_leq_1p10x_and_zero_eplan003_and_maintain_lt_full).

